EXPERIMENT 35 – HANDLING JAVASCRIPT ALERT, CONFIRM AND PROMPT USING SELENIUM
AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to handle JavaScript alert, confirm and prompt pop-ups.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the selenium-java (Selenium 4) dependency to pom.xml.
2. Selenium Manager downloads the browser driver automatically.
3. Open the JavaScript alerts page.
4. Click the JS Alert button, switch to the alert using driver.switchTo().alert(), print its text and accept it.
5. Click the JS Confirm button and dismiss it.
6. Click the JS Prompt button, enter text using sendKeys() and accept it.
7. Read the result text displayed after every pop-up and verify it.
8. Close the browser and stop.
CODE
Exercise35.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;

public class Exercise35 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            driver.get("https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/javascript_alerts");

            driver.findElement(By.xpath(
                "//button[text()='Click for JS Alert']"
            )).click();

            Alert alert = driver.switchTo().alert();

            System.out.println("Alert text : " + alert.getText());
            alert.accept();

            System.out.println("Result : " +
                driver.findElement(By.id("result")).getText());

            driver.findElement(By.xpath(
                "//button[text()='Click for JS Confirm']"
            )).click();

            alert = driver.switchTo().alert();

            System.out.println("Confirm text : " + alert.getText());
            alert.dismiss();

            System.out.println("Result : " +
                driver.findElement(By.id("result")).getText());

            driver.findElement(By.xpath(
                "//button[text()='Click for JS Prompt']"
            )).click();

            alert = driver.switchTo().alert();
            alert.sendKeys("Hello Selenium");
            alert.accept();

            System.out.println("Result : " +
                driver.findElement(By.id("result")).getText());

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
Pop-up Type	Action
JavaScript Alert	Accept
JavaScript Confirm	Dismiss
JavaScript Prompt	Enter Hello Selenium and accept

OUTPUT
Alert text   : I am a JS Alert
Result       : You successfully clicked an alert
Confirm text : I am a JS Confirm
Result       : You clicked: Cancel
Result       : You entered: Hello Selenium


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to handle JavaScript alert, confirm and prompt pop-ups was executed successfully and the output was verified.
